You're right to question this. Looking at the current tspec.toml:

```toml
[[linker]]
args = ["-static", "-nostdlib", "-nodefaultlibs", "-e_start", ...]
```

Everything is in `Args`. The other variants (`Static`, `NoStdlib`, `Entry`, `GcSections`) exist in `types.rs` but aren't used in practice.

So `generate_build_rs` really only needs:

```rust
fn generate_build_rs(path: &Path, crate_name: &str, spec: &Spec) -> Result<()> {
    let mut lines = vec![
        "// Generated by xt - do not edit".to_string(),
        "fn main() {".to_string(),
    ];

    for param in &spec.linker {
        if let LinkerParam::Args(args) = param {
            for arg in args {
                lines.push(format!(
                    "    println!(\"cargo:rustc-link-arg-bin={}={}\");",
                    crate_name, arg
                ));
            }
        }
    }

    lines.push("}".to_string());
    fs::write(path, lines.join("\n"))?;
    Ok(())
}
```

The other variants are dead code we could remove from types.rs, or keep for potential future structured specs. Want me to simplify to just `Args`?

